#  8. Taking User Input

Python allows programs to interact with users.

```python
name = input("Enter your name: ")

print("Hello", name)
print("Welcome to Python!")
```

Example:

```text
Enter your name: Vihari
Hello Vihari
Welcome to Python!
```

### Important

`input()` normally returns data as a **string**.

For numbers:

```python
age = int(input("Enter your age: "))

print("Your age is:", age)
```

